drivers/flash: program the QSPI chip-select high time in its DCR field

The HAL ORs QSPI_InitTypeDef.ChipSelectHighTime into QUADSPI_DCR as is
and expects one of the shifted QSPI_CS_HIGH_TIME_* values. The driver
passed the bare cycle count minus one, so CSHT always stayed at one
cycle and the low bits landed in CKMODE: cs-high-time = <6> programmed
DCR 0x...0001, chip select high for 1 cycle (9 ns at 108 MHz, under the
N25Q128A's deselect time) and clock mode 3, where 6 cycles in mode 0
were asked for. Shift the value into the CSHT field.

diff --git a/drivers/flash/flash_stm32_qspi.c b/drivers/flash/flash_stm32_qspi.c
index ec4fe7706e8..0e9610c0cbc 100644
--- a/drivers/flash/flash_stm32_qspi.c
+++ b/drivers/flash/flash_stm32_qspi.c
@@ -1631,7 +1631,11 @@ static int flash_stm32_qspi_init(const struct device *dev)
 	 */
 	dev_data->hqspi.Init.FlashSize = 27U;
 #endif
-	dev_data->hqspi.Init.ChipSelectHighTime = dev_cfg->cs_high_time - 1;
+	/* The HAL ORs this field into DCR as is: it takes the shifted CSHT
+	 * value (QSPI_CS_HIGH_TIME_*), not a cycle count.
+	 */
+	dev_data->hqspi.Init.ChipSelectHighTime = (dev_cfg->cs_high_time - 1)
+						  << QUADSPI_DCR_CSHT_Pos;
 #if STM32_QSPI_DOUBLE_FLASH
 	dev_data->hqspi.Init.DualFlash = QSPI_DUALFLASH_ENABLE;
 
